stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Armed: RT1 trigger arms at its lead time or its event fires
    Armed --> Assigned: RT2 assigned to a re-checker who is not the last grader
    Assigned --> InProgress: RT3 re-checker opens the source
    InProgress --> BlockedFetch: RT4 the fetch fails - tool and vantage recorded
    BlockedFetch --> InProgress: RT5 retry with a different method or tool
    BlockedFetch --> Escalated: RT6 attempts exhausted or band deadline passes
    InProgress --> OutcomeRecorded: RT7 held, changed, killed or no successor
    InProgress --> Escalated: RT6 band deadline passes with no outcome
    Escalated --> InProgress: RT8 owner role reassigns or supplies a method
    OutcomeRecorded --> Closed: RT9 grading event written and consumers acknowledge
    Closed --> Armed: RT10 the trigger re-arms with its next date or event
    Closed --> [*]: the row is killed and the trigger retires

    note right of BlockedFetch
        A blocked fetch never closes a task.
        The row keeps its grade.
        The daily lint reports it.
    end note

    note right of OutcomeRecorded
        Silence is a recorded outcome.
        No successor found is written,
        with the date and the re-checker.
    end note
